ww.dw.com/en/the-lawyer-of-junaid-hafeez-a-fullbright-scholar-imprisoned-for-13-years-in-a-pakistani-jail-tells-dw-he-is-hopeful-for-his-release/a-79490207?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A former Fullbright scholar, Junaid Hafeez was sentenced to death under Pakistan's controversial blasphemy laws. His family and lawyer told DW there is now hope a court will overturn the conviction.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea: Lost shark draws over half a million visitors</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5fa63f1d3d63a4b243d21fbaf30546396b15bbd5246b5720bfd81d6c12cea15c</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:01:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T09:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-lost-shark-draws-over-half-a-million-visitors/a-79482014--618815d2f667.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-lost-shark-draws-over-half-a-million-visitors/a-79482014?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The South Korean port of Busan says that a stranded shark has become a major tourist draw. It's also named the ocean predator an honorary ambassador to the city.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Key opposition leaders meet to discuss poll body row</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:80646c60d743bb8798397d8ada1de70cb1c3bdc243269adf77a2f1425411a949</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:01:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T08:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-key-opposition-leaders-meet-to-discuss-poll-body-row/live-79481549--3920f917ca04.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-key-opposition-leaders-meet-to-discuss-poll-body-row/live-79481549?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">India's opposition leaders meet in New Delhi to push back against voter roll revisions and discuss poll body chief Gyanesh Kumar. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>North Korea denies South's claim, calls DMZ blast a 'farce'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6d0fc42eae230f3bb64babe88ab653383f517deb40edd10517d9a671196818cf</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T04:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-korea-denies-south-s-claim-calls-dmz-blast-a-farce/a-79481164--66024b7f40bf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-korea-denies-south-s-claim-calls-dmz-blast-a-farce/a-79481164?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">North Korean leader Kim Jong Un's sister Kim Yo Jong has accused Seoul of conspiracy after it blamed Pyongyang for the blast in the DMZ.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>North Korea has recently completed two road bridges easing transport to strategic allies Russia and China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:32b6364eb60b241f4a1c766784daed2445f33576d15b276e8ac8ec1b69d3ac36</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T13:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-korea-has-recently-completed-two-road-bridges-easing-transport-to-strategic-allies-russia-and-/a-79473981--09998bc65869.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-korea-has-recently-completed-two-road-bridges-easing-transport-to-strategic-allies-russia-and-china/a-79473981?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two recently opened bridges are expected to ease trade and transport between North Korea and its powerful neighbors. The new connections come as Pyongyang builds strategic ties with China and Russia.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Women and children displaced by Nepal's floods say safe housing, privacy and stability remain out of reach</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae3f0b02e37b702af046f0b2b434d0214372570718592d22912b045d54c91255</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T13:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/women-and-children-displaced-by-nepal-s-floods-say-safe-housing-privacy-and-stability-remain-out-of-/a-79474014--5ad51afec87b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/women-and-children-displaced-by-nepal-s-floods-say-safe-housing-privacy-and-stability-remain-out-of-reach/a-79474014?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Families living in temporary shelters in northern Nepal say safety and privacy remain out of reach as concerns about trafficking and abuse mount.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Global trade weathers Iran, Ukraine and Trump's tariffs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dd13b8a07c7a543d98dd011a38adddf7879bfd2855a29fe75b1317bfab279448</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T10:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/global-trade-weathers-iran-ukraine-and-trump-s-tariffs/a-79352643--538fe77d9a72.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/global-trade-weathers-iran-ukraine-and-trump-s-tariffs/a-79352643?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Over the past six years, COVID, two wars and Donald Trump's tariffs have shaken world trade. With globalization already stalling, is this a temporary shock or the start of a great reversal?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Malaysia repatriates Myanmar migrants despite UN warnings</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2b14f3b8e9cd840f67e34eb203b677e3ab2cded30704205e334f08536c55df8f</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T10:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/malaysia-repatriates-myanmar-migrants-despite-un-warnings/a-79470814--e0fb5ad7aea0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/malaysia-repatriates-myanmar-migrants-despite-un-warnings/a-79470814?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Malaysia has started repatriating about 1,500 Myanmar nationals, defying warnings from the UN and rights groups. Malaysia, facing an uptick in anti-migrant sentiment, says the program is strictly voluntary.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea's gender pay gap grows as women get older</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:34f87e0513bb8c948aa6e73881276f010d4ad7d2ef1e4ff3fce95fdc467df1d9</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T10:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-s-gender-pay-gap-grows-as-women-get-older/a-79431285--9ddac1458d8e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-s-gender-pay-gap-grows-as-women-get-older/a-79431285?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new report shows how in South Korea, women on average earn less and have fewer employment opportunities throughout their lives.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>After Xi-Trump summit, US-China rivalry remains frozen. Is this to Beijing's advantage?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5064c641ea3faf02b5f9b4107e806ec206a73768167fabc8f9c9ed753cc555e5</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T11:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/after-xi-trump-summit-us-china-rivalry-remains-frozen-is-this-to-beijing-s-advantage/a-79427127--110c4fa9d052.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/after-xi-trump-summit-us-china-rivalry-remains-frozen-is-this-to-beijing-s-advantage/a-79427127?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US president showcased White House construction projects and hosted a lavish dinner with tech CEOs, but the summit made little progress on key issues such as trade tensions and AI regulation.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Three-way battle for power in world chess: Who will be elected FIDE president in Samarkand?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:48601a0841cb6a0ed9185cbeccf6bcf0351c2e8e14ea6f0e8014f4319fa9e430</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T18:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301--bc60333e85fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The era of Russian presidents is coming to an end at the World Chess Federation (FIDE). Two Germans and one Kazakh are up for election. Among the issues at play are money, Kremlin influence, and unanswered questions.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
